Repositories (`openbinding_gateway/repositories/`): async functions that take the session, return ORM entities, import no FastAPI, never commit, and never decide who may do what.
- `repositories/jobs.py`: job lookups and listings by owner, project and retry origin; the owner filter is part of every query, and a missing row is reported by the caller.
- `repositories/organizations.py`: organization listing, direct memberships (one, listed, locked, owner count), project listing and slug check per organization, invitation lookup by token prefix, and audit events per organization; every query is filtered by the organization id it is given.
- Still in `collaboration.py`: organization/project resolution by slug or id, effective role over the ancestor chain, `require_role`/`require_project`, sponsor usage and capacity; they are tied to the authorization rules (role strength, public read, 401/403/404 choice), so they stay with the rules instead of moving into the data layer.
- Still in `access/public_read.py`: `admit_public_project`, because the public-read grant, rate limit and visibility decision are an access policy, not a lookup.
- Still in `routes/organizations.py`: the cascade delete of a project or organization, binding cases and revisions, project resources (artifact joins and visitor filtering), user and sponsor lookups through `session.get`, sponsor-wide membership counts for quotas, and `select ... for update` on the sponsor row; they are single-use or tied to a handler's transaction and rule, and moving them would only relocate code without removing duplication.
